name,address,secret,nas_type,transport
# name      : unique label (letters, digits, . _ -)
# address   : IPv4/IPv6 address or CIDR prefix (e.g. 10.20.0.0/24)
# secret    : shared secret (no commas). Leave empty to auto-generate one;
#             it is generated once, kept for re-runs, and listed in
#             /root/freeradius-client-secrets.txt.
#             Ignored for radsec (RFC 6614 fixes it to "radsec").
# nas_type  : cisco | cisco-nxos | juniper | other   (controls admin privilege attributes)
# transport : udp | radsec
core-sw1,10.0.0.1,ChangeMe-LongRandomSecret-01,cisco,udp
dc-nexus,10.0.10.0/24,,cisco-nxos,udp
edge-mx,10.0.20.1,,juniper,udp
aruba-cx-radsec,10.0.30.5,,other,radsec
